      "name": "Ramp SWE-Bench v2",
      "description": "Ramp SWE-Bench v2 is Ramp Labs' private coding benchmark of 500 backend engineering tasks built from pull requests that Ramp's in-house coding agent merged into production after engineer review, across work shipped by more than 200 Ramp engineers. Each model gets a one-shot prompt in the same sandboxed copy of Ramp's codebase and must produce a review-ready patch. A panel of LLM judges compares the candidate patch with the engineer-reviewed merged solution; a task passes when there is no material difference where the merged solution is better. Scores are pass@1 at high reasoning effort with web tools disabled, with each model running in its lab's native agent harness (Ramp's v2.1 Native view).",
